 are never wrong. *wipes memory of my mistake*<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T07:34:43-07:00","id":1443258,"title":"","content":"In third edition, the dragon blooded book says that &quot;Most of the Realm's Exalted die on the battlefield or of misadventures before their hundredth year&quot;. Which would be a weird thing to say if the majority died before their twenty-first year (still technically true in that case, but weird).<br /> It's more compatible with a situation where around 1% of dynasts die each year, so 42.56% survive 85 years (from exalting at 15 to 100). Which would imply around 7% die in secondary school. Assuming secondary school is neither dramatically more or less lethal than adulthood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T08:00:33-07:00","id":1443260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1443251#post1443251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To Exalt as a Dragon Blooded, you need to be heroic. You may be an ASSHOLE but you have to have a personal arete of some kind. Something that impresses the Four Elemental Dragons enough to give you a pass.<br /> <br /> So its no wonder most remain Dynasts as the pampered royalty of the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragon blooded also have types of proficiencies. Some just aren'y suited towards the military lifestyle. Being heroic doesn't mean they're omnicompetent especially not as children when they're learning how to do these things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T08:02:25-07:00","id":1443261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1443258#post1443258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In third edition, the dragon blooded book says that &amp;quot;Most of the Realm's Exalted die on the battlefield or of misadventures before their hundredth year&amp;quot;. Which would be a weird thing to say if the majority died before their twenty-first year (still technically true in that case, but weird).<br /> It's more compatible with a situation where around 1% of dynasts die each year, so 42.56% survive 85 years (from exalting at 15 to 100). Which would imply around 7% die in secondary school. Assuming secondary school is neither dramatically more or less lethal than adulthood.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd assume the deathrate is higher the younger they are. They have less experience, less training and have less charms. 100 years of age is when they hit their peak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T09:56:05-07:00","id":1443269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1443261#post1443261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd assume the deathrate is higher the younger they are. They have less experience, less training and have less charms. 100 years of age is when they hit their peak.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd agree it's higher the younger they are, but not a ton higher. Also, I'd guess it's lower specifically during school - the point of training for dangerous tasks is to learn about them in a less-dangerous way. My guess is the highest death rate is years 21-30, when you're first exposed to challenges that aren't carefully crafted or chosen by teachers, inexperienced and full of essence fever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T10:06:42-07:00","id":1443272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1443238#post1443238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">2. Alex is almost certainly objectively crazy. It is why he was murdered by his own men.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">As far as history goes, the idea that Alexander of Macedon died of anything other than overindulgence and poor emotional constitution is not totally falsifiable, but still not really a mainstream idea if only because there's no effective way to verify it (and the idea that he died of something mundane and arbitrary is quite believable).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1443251#post1443251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To Exalt as a Dragon Blooded, you need to be heroic. You may be an ASSHOLE but you have to have a personal arete of some kind. Something that impresses the Four Elemental Dragons enough to give you a pass.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a thing that some people have really severely wanted to be the case, but has never been portrayed in the books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T11:24:25-07:00","id":1443282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1443272#post1443272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a thing that some people have really severely wanted to be the case, but has never been portrayed in the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is how the rules go and why the Dynasts exist in the first place. There is apparently enough of a Dragonblooded &quot;shortage&quot; that a vast number of mid-level bureaucrats and one Regent exist that have the blood but never will Exalt because they don't have any sort of heroic spark to them.<br /> <br /> And arete doesn't mean you have to be a great soldier.<br /> <br /> Your greatness can be you're the greatest potter or spinning wheel maiden ever. However, you have impressed the divine SOMEHOW.<br /> <br /> I remember that guy who broke an Unconquered Sun idol because he cursed the gods and him in particular, which impressed them enough to exalt him as a Solar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-09-2021, 02:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T11:30:14-07:00","id":1443285,"title":"","content":"I'll address the other points shortly. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1443242#post1443242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And my knowledge of WW's business practices is severely lacking -- I don't know who wrote what and when without looking at book credits. I don't know anything aboit the staff's politics or private lives. But my understanding is that most of these issues of erasure (Ses in Wonders, Kes's sex life, Gervesin's infatuation) all happened before Holden was brought on as a freelancer. I don't think it necessarily holds that he'd be in a position to whistleblow.</div> </div> </div> </div> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">I'm talking more about the kind of tactics they used as developers coupled with their greater access to people who were freelancers during this period, for example </span>Stephen Lea Sheppard has developer credits for a few books in this time period so if it was a matter of company policy he'd know. If they had access to information that de-legitimised 2nd edition this much they would've let fly with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T11:56:46-07:00","id":1443287,"title":"","content":"@CTPhipps: Oh, I mean, about my point, I'm not saying that anyone has to find any of my examples admirable (I mean, it's totally fair game to say &quot;They're all a bunch of warmongering megalomaniacs and violent elites and I don't respect the lot of them and I'm quite happy dismissing them out of hand&quot;). The point was I guess I just found it a bit weird to say that anyone or any group with a reputation for winning battles wars was actually a loser/bunch of losers because their side eventually lost its wars, or their polity eventually fell; I mean, by that definition you're labelling a lot of historical generals, armies etc as &quot;losers&quot;, however successful they actually were in their lifetimes and for however long!<br /> <br /> (But, er, yeah, tangent).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T13:39:13-07:00","id":1443295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1443282#post1443282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is how the rules go</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that's neat. What book is that in?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1443282#post1443282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember that guy who broke an Unconquered Sun idol because he cursed the gods and him in particular, which impressed them enough to exalt him as a Solar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfect Soul is a woman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T13:42:02-07:00","id":1443296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1443295#post1443295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, that's neat. What book is that in?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Realm sourcebook is a good place to start.<br /> <br /> I mean, you do know that Dynasts are not Exalted as Terrestials and they are the vast majority compared to the Terrestials.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T13:42:05-07:00","id":1443297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1443261#post1443261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd assume the deathrate is higher the younger they are. They have less experience, less training and have less charms. 100 years of age is when they hit their peak.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh.<br /> <br /> Folks get over confident. They push themselves to top previous achievements. And they make more enemies.<br /> <br /> I think the death rate might be slightly higher for 30 year olds compared to 80 year old, but only slightly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T16:34:58-07:00","id":1443305,"title":"","content":"See I always assumed that previous editions had such a high mortality rate for graduates of Pasiap's Stair as a way to subtly communicate how much the Realm fucking hates letting Lost Eggs into their carefully controlled bloodlines. You're a lost egg of uncertain provenance? Great, become a monk and don't have kids or go to military school and probably die. Fuck you. Just because we promise that DBs are the elite of the earth and owed all the wealth and privilege they visibly have doesn't mean we're actually going to deliver it to the daughter of some peasants just because she catches fire one day.<br /> <br /> Is this sort of bigoted action counterproductive and visibly costing the Dynasty potentially valuable resources? <i>Yes.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":229,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","user":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","date":". 04-09-2021, 07:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T17:03:05-07:00","id":1443306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1443305#post1443305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See I always assumed that previous editions had such a high mortality rate for graduates of Pasiap's Stair as a way to subtly communicate how much the Realm fucking hates letting Lost Eggs into their carefully controlled bloodlines. You're a lost egg of uncertain provenance? Great, become a monk and don't have kids or go to military school and probably die. Fuck you. Just because we promise that DBs are the elite of the earth and owed all the wealth and privilege they visibly have doesn't mean we're actually going to deliver it to the daughter of some peasants just because she catches fire one day.<br /> <br /> Is this sort of bigoted action counterproductive and visibly costing the Dynasty potentially valuable resources? <i>Yes.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I always thought that the house of bells and pasiap's stair were just places that try to prune the people who are able to excel in an actual battlefield compared to the people who just aren't as good. Pasiap's Stair, from the 1e depiction anyway, made it seem like they wanted these outcastes to be valuable resources but they had to be completely broken and remade. When someone was such a failure that they couldn't hack it and that the beatings weren't getting through, they'd throw someone off the peak of the cliff. Something they didn't do lightly. It's just part of the issue with the realm treating dragon blooded as pawns in the end. Those that survive deserve it. Those that don't, were too weak to prove anything of use to the realm. The ability to switch secondary schools doesn't even exist for realm dragon blooded. You either dropped out of them, died or succeeded. Dropouts were mostly treated with extreme contempt unless they managed to do something that was of benefit to their family.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-09-2021, 08:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-10T08:48:19-07:00","id":1443369,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately, that's <i>still </i>a pretty shitty model for getting &quot;excellent&quot; Dragon-Blooded at the end; you keep saying it's &quot;just part of the issue,&quot; but this is something <i>the Realm chose to do</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-10T14:56:35-07:00","id":1443405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1443369#post1443369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately, that's <i>still </i>a pretty shitty model for getting &quot;excellent&quot; Dragon-Blooded at the end; you keep saying it's &quot;just part of the issue,&quot; but this is something <i>the Realm chose to do</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the question is how bad do you want the Realm Terrestials to be? For me the fact they're a eugenicist, classicist, imperialistic, infighting bunch of assholes is the point.<br /> <br /> But they shouldn't be homophobic or sexist because Mama Scarlet wouldn't stand for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-10T15:19:41-07:00","id":1443411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1443405#post1443405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the question is how bad do you want the Realm Terrestials to be? For me the fact they're a eugenicist, classicist, imperialistic, infighting bunch of assholes is the point.<br /> <br /> But they shouldn't be homophobic or sexist because Mama Scarlet wouldn't stand for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think she cares but I do think both those things disrupt the balance. In 1e the only time homosexuality was an issue as when it interfered with producing children. Sexism wasn't really there because the dragon blooded are a meritocracy where anyone can be anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-10T15:28:53-07:00","id":1443412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1443411#post1443411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think she cares but I do think both those things disrupt the balance. In 1e the only time homosexuality was an issue as when it interfered with producing children. Sexism wasn't really there because the dragon blooded are a meritocracy where anyone can be anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's a deeply misleading statement.<br /> <br /> I'd say it's more: The Dragonblooded are an oligarchy where <b>Terrestial Exalted of Proper Noble Blood </b>can <b>theoretically</b> rise in the ranks if they play the game of favors correctly as well as have their families support.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-10T16:23:55-07:00","id":1443420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1443412#post1443412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that's a deeply misleading statement.<br /> <br /> I'd say it's more: The Dragonblooded are an oligarchy where <b>Terrestial Exalted of Proper Noble Blood </b>can <b>theoretically</b> rise in the ranks if they play the game of favors correctly as well as have their families support.</div> </div> </div> </div>Family can only do so much. if you aren't capable of doing your job or excelling no amount of family pull will support you. In fact, they'll probably be so embarrassed at your failure they'll send you off to a remote location where you can't do more damage to their family reputation. It's required that a dragon blooded work towards the job he wants and if he fails his family won't just support him. They didn't raise him just so he could be a burden on them. Now nepotism does exist but only because families are putting their kids in those positions because they need them to get information or they need to favor them over other houses for political or material reasons. Which is why the family pressures marriage so much. More marriage=more kids=more pawns in your game of politics. It's why they don't care if they lose a few kids if most of the ones who are alive are smarter and better for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-10T16:47:37-07:00","id":1443422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1443420#post1443420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Family can only do so much. if you aren't capable of doing your job or excelling no amount of family pull will support you. In fact, they'll probably be so embarrassed at your failure they'll send you off to a remote location where you can't do more damage to their family reputation. It's required that a dragon blooded work towards the job he wants and if he fails his family won't just support him. They didn't raise him just so he could be a burden on them. Now nepotism does exist but only because families are putting their kids in those positions because they need them to get information or they need to favor them over other houses for political or material reasons. Which is why the family pressures marriage so much. More marriage=more kids=more pawns in your game of politics. It's why they don't care if they lose a few kids if most of the ones who are alive are smarter and better for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's a bit more of a gray area there while not discounting your point entirely. There's ample places in the Realm where you send your dysfunctional kids, up to and including military schools that could theoretically kill them. Part of what is notable about the Exalted running about the Realm is that unless they decide to head to the Blessed Isle, they're not going to be running into the best and brightest of the Dragonblooded or even Dynasts. The realm doesn't waste even if very few are able to rise to the highest of ranks and even then, the lowest ranks of the Realm's bloodlines are far above the most competent of those outside it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-11T01:41:15-07:00","id":1443451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1443412#post1443412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that's a deeply misleading statement.<br /> <br /> I'd say it's more: The Dragonblooded are an oligarchy where <b>Terrestial Exalted of Proper Noble Blood </b>can <b>theoretically</b> rise in the ranks if they play the game of favors correctly as well as have their families support.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think areas of the Realm are a meritocracy.<br /> <br /> The Imperial Legions were a strict meritocracy, where Outcast Saloy Hin became a general (right off the bat in 1E and in every edition since). <br /> <br /> Amon Mora isn't a Dynast (3E). I'd be surprised if the majority of the Crown Marshals are Dynasts.<br /> <br /> Likewise, the Immaculate Order is pretty accessible and based around breaking the ties to your old life. Dynasts have it easier to sign up (easier to become a monk if you're not going to be put to death for quitting, much easier to become a monk if you're already educated and your family isn't going to starve to death because your not working the family farm), but not necessarily to advance.<br /> <br /> The ventures of the Great Houses (the Imperial Navy, House Legions, Satrapy system) are all nepotic oligarchies. The entire system of tribute, taxation, government and law is an oligarchy (it's an empire ruled by a dynasty).<br /> <br /> 1E presents us with a Realm that kills children who don't live up to their parents expectations. 2/3E softened that a little, but it's still a place where great things are expected of &quot;great people&quot;. That said:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1443422#post1443422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think there's a bit more of a gray area there while not discounting your point entirely. There's ample places in the Realm where you send your dysfunctional kids, up to and including military schools that could theoretically kill them. Part of what is notable about the Exalted running about the Realm is that unless they decide to head to the Blessed Isle, they're not going to be running into the best and brightest of the Dragonblooded or even Dynasts. The realm doesn't waste even if very few are able to rise to the highest of ranks and even then, the lowest ranks of the Realm's bloodlines are far above the most competent of those outside it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. This. I agree almost entirely with this.<br /> <br /> Some of the Realms most ambitious aristocracy can be found outside of the Blessed Isle, though. That doesn't necessarily translate to the &quot;best and brightest&quot;, but there is some overlap in that Venn diagram.<br /> <br /> The Realm's brightest know there's something rotten in the state of Denmark. And there are more than a few looking outward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T06:24:55-07:00","id":1443589,"title":"","content":"To go back to the original thread topic, and about DB marriage specifically: remember for lengthy periods of human history in a number of cultures, marriage was (a) mostly a thing nobility did and (b) mostly about inheritance and alliances. That's not to say other people didn't couple up and form family units, but even then you might rely on matchmakers to find a spouse. It's something that still happens in Japan today, although it's a small minority of marriages now. (Heck, if we want to be extremely generous, what are OKCupid and the like other than modern-day matchmakers?)<br /> <br /> Still, not marrying for love (or at least, not marrying <i>due</i> to love) is not the same thing as &quot;force two people who will not ever get along together&quot;, but it's also why even the current 3e Realm probably has more male-female couples who, if their orientations and preferences lie outside of that, take on lovers than same-sex couples who are formally married; from the Dynastic perspective so long as you tolerate your spouse and do your duty of producing children, what you do otherwise can be accepted. I imagine the 'happy' sort of Dynastic marriage involves two people who find each other acceptable and might actually grow love over the course of their marriage as they gain trust in their spouse.<br /> <br /> Reading between the lines while 2e never had any top-down &quot;remove all the gay people!&quot; mandate, John Chambers seemed to put Exalted way down his list of priorities and gave more direction to Scion. I imagine this left a lot of room for homophobic or just unthinking freelancers to roll back things that weren't caught. It certainly left a lot of room for absolutely ludicrous holes in the <i>mechanics</i>, after all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> See the &quot;Realm is a matriarchy&quot; thing - no, the explicit word &quot;matriarchy&quot; was not used. However, it was stated to be &quot;a lot like the modern world, but gender-flipped with a bias towards women&quot;. Most writers unthinkingly still went with Default Males, and I think the 3e use of matriarchy and matriarchs is <i>extremely</i> fair even if you still go &quot;like our world but flipped&quot;. Patriarchy's still a thing, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T07:29:30-07:00","id":1443593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1443589#post1443589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See the &quot;Realm is a matriarchy&quot; thing - no, the explicit word &quot;matriarchy&quot; was not used. However, it was stated to be &quot;a lot like the modern world, but gender-flipped with a bias towards women&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay... which Exalted book prior to 3E said the Realm was like the modern world but flipped?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most writers unthinkingly still went with Default Males, and I think the 3e use of matriarchy and matriarchs is <i>extremely</i> fair even if you still go &quot;like our world but flipped&quot;. Patriarchy's still a thing, after all. </div> </div> </div>Sure, but I don't think that's egregious in terms of how past editions represented the Realm.<br /> <br /> If I write a setting with three female CEOs and two male CEOs, that's not unrealistic because &quot;patriarchy is still a thing&quot;. If I write a setting with a male president with a female vice president, that doesn't mean my setting is free of sexism.<br /> <br /> If you have a patriarchy under law, where women can't leave the house, or own property, or testify in court... then writing 3/5 of your nation's top military brass as women doesn't make sense.<br /> <br /> But if your nation is theoretically equal, even if there is persistent gender bias, I don't see why you couldn't have women in positions of authority.<br /> <br /> The company I work IRL for has seven people on the board. Five of them (including the CEO and the COO) are women. But our gender pay gap is nearly 40%. Four-zero. Forty. That's as many as four tens.<br /> <br /> Just because 1E and 2E wrote a bunch of male characters, that doesn't mean those characters didn't face discrimination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 04-12-2021, 11:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T15:16:23-07:00","id":1443659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1443593#post1443593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay... which Exalted book prior to 3E said the Realm was like the modern world but flipped?</div> </div> </div> </div>... Exalted: the Dragon-blooded? The sidebar that's been mentioned before? If you're asking &quot;did it literally use those exact words&quot;, no, but I wasn't quoting. The concept is one that has been used as a simile many times by both writers and fans based on that sidebar, however.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sure, but I don't think that's egregious in terms of how past editions represented the Realm.<br /> <br /> If I write a setting with three female CEOs and two male CEOs, that's not unrealistic because &quot;patriarchy is still a thing&quot;. If I write a setting with a male president with a female vice president, that doesn't mean my setting is free of sexism.<br /> <br /> If you have a patriarchy under law, where women can't leave the house, or own property, or testify in court... then writing 3/5 of your nation's top military brass as women doesn't make sense.<br /> <br /> But if your nation is theoretically equal, even if there is persistent gender bias, I don't see why you couldn't have women in positions of authority.<br /> <br /> The company I work IRL for has seven people on the board. Five of them (including the CEO and the COO) are women. But our gender pay gap is nearly 40%. Four-zero. Forty. That's as many as four tens.<br /> <br /> Just because 1E and 2E wrote a bunch of male characters, that doesn't mean those characters didn't face discrimination. </div> </div> </div>No, but the thing about a fictional setting is readers can only judge by what they were given. We are told that there are many kingdoms and countries and cultures in a single square inch of Creation's map, and then 2e went and only used places mentioned in 1e and only had them interact with other places, even if they were <i>thousands of miles apart</i>.<br /> <br /> Similarly, if you're talking about a culture where women dominate and men face a glass ceiling, <i>you damn well better show women in positions of power, and have them tend to show up more often than men!</i><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T18:05:38-07:00","id":1443680,"title":"","content":"At the end of the day in 1st and 2nd edition, throughout the entire gamelines we got a handful of throw-away lines about how there was discrimination against men in the Realm, but then it was never actually demonstrated or presented outside of those lines. It would be very, very easy for someone to read through all of 1st or 2nd edition and never even realize that there was even supposed to be discrimination of any sort against males in the Realm. So for many people who went through both editions the idea in 3rd edition that there was persistent discrimination against men in the Realm was something that seems extremely new and different because it was something that had only ever had the most minor and insignificant wordcount devoted to it in the earlier editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T19:54:37-07:00","id":1443686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1443680#post1443680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the end of the day in 1st and 2nd edition, throughout the entire gamelines we got a handful of throw-away lines about how there was discrimination against men in the Realm, but then it was never actually demonstrated or presented outside of those lines. It would be very, very easy for someone to read through all of 1st or 2nd edition and never even realize that there was even supposed to be discrimination of any sort against males in the Realm. So for many people who went through both editions the idea in 3rd edition that there was persistent discrimination against men in the Realm was something that seems extremely new and different because it was something that had only ever had the most minor and insignificant wordcount devoted to it in the earlier editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn't just that it was a few throwaway lines but also that everything else went against it. Dragon blooded made house heads an equal half and half. Most of the throwaway lines weren't even necessarily discriminatory in nature. 3rd definitely makes it a bigger deal then it had to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-12-2021, 11:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T01:49:58-07:00","id":1443716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1443659#post1443659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ... Exalted: the Dragon-blooded? The sidebar that's been mentioned before? If you're asking &quot;did it literally use those exact words&quot;, no, but I wasn't quoting. </div> </div> </div> </div>You weren't quoting when you put your point in quotes.<br /> And you're referring to the sidebar that explicitly states that the Realm has no gender roles and that from Dynasts to slaves there's gender equality and that how your character being Exalted is far more important than where they wear their genitals? That sidebar? The sidebar that begins &quot;gender takes a back seat to position in the Perfected Heirachy&quot; and ends &quot;the fact that a character is one of the Dragon-Blooded will have a much greater impact than their gender in Realm society&quot;.<br /> <br /> That's the sidebar that makes you think the presentation of 1E and 2E was wrong for not featuring women dominating society?<br /> <br /> Because the sidebar doesn't say what you seem to think it says.<br /> <br /> It doesn't say &quot;real life isn't sexist and neither is the Realm!&quot; It makes no comparison with sexism in real life. It says the Dynasty educates all its scions in leadership equally and this attitude is pervasive in society right down to slaves -- who don't have gender roles. What sex based discrimination that does exist is not a genuine limit, instead men are seen as irresponsible and paid slightly less. That's the society we're presented with.<br /> <br /> [Edit]<br /> <br /> Now I'm not saying you can't interpret the text the way you have. We all draw our own inferences, and you've not done anything crazy. You've just applied the filter of your own lived experience. Same as dozens of other folks. Perfectly reasonable. Folks who used to write for 2E have said the Realm was meant to be a matriarchy but it just never made it to text. I have never written for Exalted. I have no special insight. I can't tell you what was supposed to be in the books or how we were supposed to interpret the text.<br /> <br /> All I can do is tell you what the text actually says, and how I interpreted the text.<br /> <br /> I didn't add words that weren't there. The text doesn't say &quot;matriarchy&quot; and it doesn't say &quot;like real life USA circa 2001 but gender flipped&quot;. Maybe we were supposed to infer that, but that's not what the text says.<br /> <br /> I did interpret it based on the context given by the rest of the book. Maybe that was a mistake. Maybe poor editing and multiple writers meant the published text was wrong. But taking it in context... the Realm was consistently portrayed across two editions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1443680#post1443680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the end of the day in 1st and 2nd edition, throughout the entire gamelines we got a handful of throw-away lines</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, what books where these lines in?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1443686#post1443686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It wasn't just that it was a few throwaway lines but also that everything else went against it. Dragon blooded made house heads an equal half and half. Most of the throwaway lines weren't even necessarily discriminatory in nature. 3rd definitely makes it a bigger deal then it had to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the 3E presentation. I prefer the 3E presentation. It seems to fit people's headcanon better.<br /> <br /> But the 3E presentation <i>is</i> markedly something new. It's not fixing the broken presentation of past editions, because past editions never made the claim.<br /> <br /> The 1E sidebar being used to claim this is an old idea said both girls and boys are equally groomed for leadership, immediately after showing Great Houses with a 50:50 gender split in leadership, after using deliberately gender neutral language (&quot;founder&quot;, &quot;head&quot;, &quot;elder of the House&quot; and &quot;members of note&quot;, never &quot;matriarch&quot;). Exalted The Dragon-Blooded showed us a gender neutral society, then had a sidebar on how Realm society is gender neutral. And somehow we're arguing about what a bad job it did of portraying a female dominated society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 04-13-2021, 05:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T15:46:24-07:00","id":1443807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1443716#post1443716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the 3E presentation. I prefer the 3E presentation. It seems to fit people's headcanon better.<br /> <br /> But the 3E presentation <i>is</i> markedly something new. It's not fixing the broken presentation of past editions, because past editions never made the claim.<br /> <br /> The 1E sidebar being used to claim this is an old idea said both girls and boys are equally groomed for leadership, immediately after showing Great Houses with a 50:50 gender split in leadership, after using deliberately gender neutral language (&quot;founder&quot;, &quot;head&quot;, &quot;elder of the House&quot; and &quot;members of note&quot;, never &quot;matriarch&quot;). Exalted The Dragon-Blooded showed us a gender neutral society, then had a sidebar on how Realm society is gender neutral. And somehow we're arguing about what a bad job it did of portraying a female dominated society.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I like 1e way more but I agree with what you said. The realm was matrilineal in the past but I wouldn't have called it a matriarchy simply because it wasn't presented as such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-13-2021, 07:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T21:16:02-07:00","id":1443836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1443807#post1443807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I like 1e way more but I agree with what you said. The realm was matrilineal in the past but I wouldn't have called it a matriarchy simply because it wasn't presented as such.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think of the Realm as a Matriarchy save in the Thatcher sense that a woman was its head for the majority of its existence.<br /> <br /> The Scarlet Empress favored her children and their children but otherwise was probably fairly neutral about the sex business. If there was a bias, it's the fact that in addition to the Scarlet Empress the second most powerful person in the Empire was also a woman (Mnemon).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T04:52:30-07:00","id":1443863,"title":"","content":"And the Mouth of Peace. (Even if the Mouth of Peace's 1E presentation was... not protagonising.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T07:39:07-07:00","id":1443877,"title":"","content":"I'm mildly on the side of 1e Realm (with its flaw/merit of &quot;edginess&quot;, more self-involved politics, and where gender bias is more &quot;Your audience with the Empress probably goes a bit better on average&quot; rather than actual gender division of labour or hierarchy). But then I would be.<br /> <br /> That said! The 3e matriarchy idea does really complement the longstanding theme (term used lightly) of Exalted where powerful people, and the Empress in the Realm particularly, have an hyper-enhanced power to determine the direction of societies in different directions in a way that is reminiscent of but perhaps much greater than any real Great Person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T13:22:38-07:00","id":1443923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1443863#post1443863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the Mouth of Peace. (Even if the Mouth of Peace's 1E presentation was... not protagonising.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, she's Chejop's hand puppet.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T17:05:40-07:00","id":1443952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1443305#post1443305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See I always assumed that previous editions had such a high mortality rate for graduates of Pasiap's Stair as a way to subtly communicate how much the Realm fucking hates letting Lost Eggs into their carefully controlled bloodlines. You're a lost egg of uncertain provenance? Great, become a monk and don't have kids or go to military school and probably die. Fuck you. Just because we promise that DBs are the elite of the earth and owed all the wealth and privilege they visibly have doesn't mean we're actually going to deliver it to the daughter of some peasants just because she catches fire one day.<br /> <br /> Is this sort of bigoted action counterproductive and visibly costing the Dynasty potentially valuable resources? <i>Yes.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Problem is that's really not a very good place to be subtle.<br /> Training with a ridiculous rate of fatalities being considered superior to conventional methods despite that is something of a genre clich\u00e9\u2026 like seriously, most of Warhammer 40k does this without a hint of irony. If people who were playing a Coin outcaste didn\u2019t see this as an expression the Scarlet Dynasty wanted them dead, then that was this lore failing to serve its primary purpose. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T22:07:55-07:00","id":1443982,"title":"","content":"It is almost as though they wanted to give Outcastes a backstory of resentment as a reason to rebel against the Realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T04:20:25-07:00","id":1444013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1443982#post1443982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is almost as though they wanted to give Outcastes a backstory of resentment as a reason to rebel against the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but the presentation of Pasiap's Stair has always been that it's good at producing loyal soldiers. It's just that they were loyal to the Realm and the Empress which has lead to them being removed from command roles by nepotism or forced to choose sides by the upcoming civil war.<br /> <br /> If we're instead reading Pasiap's Stair graduates as the resentful survivors of a &quot;school&quot; where students are murdered by each other and the instructors with 2/3rds dying before they join the Legions, that's a <i>very</i> different take on things and the Great House leaders wanting to take power from these people is pretty reasonable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T08:54:58-07:00","id":1444036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1443863#post1443863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the Mouth of Peace. (Even if the Mouth of Peace's 1E presentation was... not protagonising.)</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1443923#post1443923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, she's Chejop's hand puppet.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Mouth of Peace presentation in First Edition consisted of more than just one line in a Sidereals chapter fiction, and even within that scope &quot;how addled she must be from all the sorceries at work upon her mind&quot; doesn't quite directly lead to a reading of &quot;absolute puppet of Chejop&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T12:20:22-07:00","id":1444050,"title":"","content":"The presentation of Sidereal mind-control magic in 1e was that it replaced your will to question them with their own and eventually turned your brain to jelly, so it's not hard to see where that sentiment might arise, at least with regard to Cult of the Illuminated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T15:56:49-07:00","id":1444081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1444013#post1444013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but the presentation of Pasiap's Stair has always been that it's good at producing loyal soldiers. It's just that they were loyal to the Realm and the Empress which has lead to them being removed from command roles by nepotism or forced to choose sides by the upcoming civil war.<br /> <br /> If we're instead reading Pasiap's Stair graduates as the resentful survivors of a &quot;school&quot; where students are murdered by each other and the instructors with 2/3rds dying before they join the Legions, that's a <i>very</i> different take on things and the Great House leaders wanting to take power from these people is pretty reasonable.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a place where they are brainwashed and turned into a loyal soldier. It honeys it's words a bit but it's still very clear that they break people down in order to build them up which is why it's so brutal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T04:31:26-07:00","id":1444155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1444081#post1444081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a place where they are brainwashed and turned into a loyal soldier. It honeys it's words a bit but it's still very clear that they break people down in order to build them up which is why it's so brutal.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that kind of approach tends to produce the exact opposite results. After all, in such a model, it's the people with the <i>weakest</i> will that are most likely to survive. Or those that can pretend the best they have been broken.<br /> <br /> So, you produce either loyal but mediocre soldiers, whose loyalty is not so strong it cannot be subverted later, loyal ones that cannot be subverted, but only because they lost most of their individuality (and initiative), or ticking bombs that you <i>think</i> are loyal, but probably hate you and all you stand for instead.<br /> <br /> Those are not very promising results.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T04:49:11-07:00","id":1444162,"title":"","content":"And another thing. These are exalts. They get angry. They get pissed mad. I know that some might disagree, but every single DB is a <b>hero</b>. They don't take shit lying down. <br /> <br /> Ok, sure? You wanna beat down on them? They run. They figure out plans. They get sick of it and run guerilla warfare on your nearby towns and places, or decide that yes, 'fuck the Realm!'. You get a hot-shit instructor? Well, half a dozen outcastes come after you at night and tear you to pieces, because these are DBs, and they are heroes. <br /> <br /> So you're going to have constant clashes between Instructors trying to beat them down and angry Outcaste students trying to punch back. Because if some bog-standard DB can beat down a younger hero of the Dragons, the Elemental Dragons wasted their time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T08:57:43-07:00","id":1444212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1444155#post1444155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that kind of approach tends to produce the exact opposite results. After all, in such a model, it's the people with the <i>weakest</i> will that are most likely to survive. Or those that can pretend the best they have been broken.<br /> <br /> So, you produce either loyal but mediocre soldiers, whose loyalty is not so strong it cannot be subverted later, loyal ones that cannot be subverted, but only because they lost most of their individuality (and initiative), or ticking bombs that you <i>think</i> are loyal, but probably hate you and all you stand for instead.<br /> <br /> Those are not very promising results.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. My problem is when Warhammer 40,000 has lore like this such as with the Schola Progenium the intent is to maintain the grimdark aesthetic of the wargame and you're not supposed to overthink it.<br /> <br /> For a roleplay game where you\u2019re supposed to occupy the headspace of a character who went through that, \u201cbrainwashing\u201d is a lacklustre and incomplete explanation for why they hold the beliefs that they do.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T17:01:33-07:00","id":1444274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1444155#post1444155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that kind of approach tends to produce the exact opposite results. After all, in such a model, it's the people with the <i>weakest</i> will that are most likely to survive. Or those that can pretend the best they have been broken.<br /> <br /> So, you produce either loyal but mediocre soldiers, whose loyalty is not so strong it cannot be subverted later, loyal ones that cannot be subverted, but only because they lost most of their individuality (and initiative), or ticking bombs that you <i>think</i> are loyal, but probably hate you and all you stand for instead.<br /> <br /> Those are not very promising results.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean a lot goes into raising an outcaste. They don't just get told the coin or the razor. They get indoctrinated for several years before they have to make that choice. They get trained to read, write, get teaching and get all the privilege a dragon blooded. The harsh training can be internally justified as necessary and the benefits of the training make those who survive some of the best in realm.. There's also the fact that people can make it to 100 years of age, then join the inner realm society. Which for someone who started as a peasant or outside the threshold is a massive status jump. However, you do have people who rebel. One of the named outcastes in the first book was an outcaste general who decided to defect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T20:12:01-07:00","id":1444286,"title":"","content":"\u201cHow dumb is it to kill most of your officer cadets?\u201d sounds like a GREAT new thread topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T12:20:29-07:00","id":1444369,"title":"","content":"As someone who started 2nd edition and still haven't read parts of 1E I can confirm that I never realized Ophilis Ses was either gay or bi and otherwise fell for some of the other things mentioned that tried to sweep a 1E characters homosexual traits under the rug.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 04-17-2021, 03:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T03:02:55-07:00","id":1444476,"title":"","content":"I'd just like to note that characters were pretty much universally more poorly described and dealt with in 2nd Edition than in 1st edition. This was because many characters only appeared in Chapter Comics in 2nd edition and there was a limit to what could be done with them there.<br /> <br /> Like Panther went from a cool and interesting character in 1st edition (my third favorite Solar in fact) to essentially a caricature of an angry, shouty, punchy, black man. To a degree that was simply due to the fact that a 2 page comic couldn't approach the nuance that chapter fiction of multi-page write ups in a Caste/Aspect could reach.<br /> <br /> Gay characters suffered even more (on top of any <i>possible</i> deliberate attempt to present them poorly) from this simply because it was often harder to try and naturally work someone's sexuality into a comic page or very short paragraph description than it was in the much larger amount of word count characters received in 1st edition.<br /> <br /> 2nd edition's approach to many characters seemed to be, &quot;Just assume the reader is already familiar with them from 1st edition.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 04-18-2021, 06:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T07:19:26-07:00","id":1444497,"title":"","content":"For my part I got cold feet over sharing my speculation over who was behind some of the more deliberate looking examples of queer erasure, I've seen things with less evidence become &quot;facts&quot; because a community was looking for a villain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T08:09:46-07:00","id":1444505,"title":"","content":"@AnubixXy, re; 2nd Edition and character, following up on your comment (and some similar comments by others in the thread earlier), I do kind of think the comics were a great idea in terms of, y'know, Exalted *is* a manga, and you want to try and convey that. But it does give some limited space for characterising internal mental states and relationships, per pagecount. It's a bit of a tradeoff to manage; if you go too much into leaning on narrative and written fiction in portraying the game and not manga-style art, you really would also fail to capture what it's about.<br /> <br /> For some context on characterisation, I do think Exalted 2e was kind of the high water mark of lots of fan conversation being like &quot;The Caste and Aspect Books were an awful and bad idea; I want to pay for gameable content for my table and not these sort of unreliable narrator microfictions that tell me what sort of characters the Exalted are&quot;. So I think there's an element there of, like, game developers responding to what the fans want. And I think that's in a sense fair in that if you're running a game, it's fair for you to want these books that give you stuff you need collected together in one place that is like &quot;The book of artefacts&quot; or &quot;The book of this region where you are setting your game&quot;. *But* the flip side of that is that if you are abandoning a book of big character portraits where authors do try to convey characters' psychology using interesting and at least somewhat subtle tricks of narrative voice, you are going to be the edition of having worse characterisation! Somewhat inevitably!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T09:34:45-07:00","id":1444516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1444476#post1444476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd just like to note that characters were pretty much universally more poorly described and dealt with in 2nd Edition than in 1st edition. This was because many characters only appeared in Chapter Comics in 2nd edition and there was a limit to what could be done with them there.<br /> <br /> Like Panther went from a cool and interesting character in 1st edition (my third favorite Solar in fact) to essentially a caricature of an angry, shouty, punchy, black man. To a degree that was simply due to the fact that a 2 page comic couldn't approach the nuance that chapter fiction of multi-page write ups in a Caste/Aspect could reach.<br /> <br /> Gay characters suffered even more (on top of any <i>possible</i> deliberate attempt to present them poorly) from this simply because it was often harder to try and naturally work someone's sexuality into a comic page or very short paragraph description than it was in the much larger amount of word count characters received in 1st edition.<br /> <br /> 2nd edition's approach to many characters seemed to be, &quot;Just assume the reader is already familiar with them from 1st edition.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I just think 2nd edition's approach was to recontextualize a lot of things. There are a lot of additions to sidereals and dragon blooded which were worse for the exalts in 2e. Oversight was my biggest bugbear and completely didn't understand what sidereals did or how they operated. Sidereals not only ensure that destiny happens but also to control destiny. The conventions are run by sidereals to dictate their vision of the future. Outside of dealing with the flaws that occur on the loom that spawn paradox, they were free to do whatever they wanted. They didn't create the scarlet empire because they were told to by the bureau of fate. They created the scarlet empire because they wanted to control destiny in to a stable but lesser pattern. Oversight just feels like it misunderstands this point and was created because people complained about their STs using Fate assassins too liberally. However, this passage doesn't fix anything, it just reduces the role of sidereals. An ST who wants to send hundreds of sidereal assassins will do it anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-18-2021, 01:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T11:59:50-07:00","id":1444529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1444505#post1444505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do think Exalted 2e was kind of the high water mark of lots of fan conversation being like &quot;The Caste and Aspect Books were an awful and bad idea; I want to pay for gameable content for my table and not these sort of unreliable narrator microfictions that tell me what sort of characters the Exalted are&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Imagine complaining about the lack of gameable content in the Caste and Aspect books and then getting 2E's Compass series with their zillions of pages about useless, made-up trivia like the bathhouse culture of Whitewall and that monastery where the Lover cursed the ghost monks to be constantly horny but unable to masturbate -.-","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T13:45:36-07:00","id":1444541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1444529#post1444529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Imagine complaining about the lack of gameable content in the Caste and Aspect books and then getting 2E's Compass series with their zillions of pages about useless, made-up trivia like the bathhouse culture of Whitewall and that monastery where the Lover cursed the ghost monks to be constantly horny but unable to masturbate -.-</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah 2e was pretty random in what it deemed worthy of preserving from 1st edition and didn't always create the connective tissue to give us a greater insight into the setting.<br /> <br /> I'll try and keep this on topic with how that related to homosexuality.<br /> <br /> Admiral Tirak\u2026 we don't know if his behaviour is illustrative of Coral's attitudes towards homosexuality or if the clandestine nature of his behaviour suggests otherwise. Like 2e Coral casually brings up throwing illegitimate children to the sharks. What is beyond the pale for a society like this?<br /> <br /> More importantly, what are its implications for a gay PC in Coral outside of running into this one guy?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T14:02:25-07:00","id":1444544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1444529#post1444529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Imagine complaining about the lack of gameable content in the Caste and Aspect books and then getting 2E's Compass series with their zillions of pages about useless, made-up trivia like the bathhouse culture of Whitewall and that monastery where the Lover cursed the ghost monks to be constantly horny but unable to masturbate -.-</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure many abyssal players 'appreciated' the monk thing giving their ST ideas on how to have the Lover punish them for failure/defiance.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T04:58:13-07:00","id":1445254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1444529#post1444529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imagine complaining about the lack of gameable content in the Caste and Aspect books and then getting 2E's Compass series with their zillions of pages about useless, made-up trivia like the bathhouse culture of Whitewall</div> </div> </div> </div>And you'd think that the <i>bathhouse </i>culture of Whitewall would be a great opportunity to tie-in to homosexuality given the RL associations.<br /> <br /> Unless ofc they did, it's been ages since I read the North Compass book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T06:00:20-07:00","id":1445257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1444529#post1444529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imagine complaining about the lack of gameable content in the Caste and Aspect books and then getting 2E's Compass series with their zillions of pages about useless, made-up trivia like the bathhouse culture of Whitewall and that monastery where the Lover cursed the ghost monks to be constantly horny but unable to masturbate -.-</div> </div> </div> </div>Useless made-up trivia? RPG setting sourcebooks are pretty much only made-up trivia and I am all here for it. Give me page upon page about bathhouses and I will eat it up. Is there even any information in <b>The Realm</b> that is not made-up trivia?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T02:42:14-07:00","id":1445455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jutlander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1445257#post1445257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Useless made-up trivia? RPG setting sourcebooks are pretty much only made-up trivia and I am all here for it. Give me page upon page about bathhouses and I will eat it up. Is there even any information in <b>The Realm</b> that is not made-up trivia?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>My (technically as yet unfinished) take from the Realm is that it prioritises information that makes life there feel vivid and can have applications in games through generating plot, either in terms of what complications arise from the place and what it has that people will compete for access over. That's also how I view the given Lunar Dominions.<br /> <br /> I find many of the Second Edition locations to be too focused on going down to the finest details of the city's features and functions, but not enough on bringing the inhabitants to life and pointing them at the future in a way for characters to take hold of or crash into.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T12:15:14-07:00","id":1445690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jutlander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1445257#post1445257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Useless made-up trivia? RPG setting sourcebooks are pretty much only made-up trivia and I am all here for it. Give me page upon page about bathhouses and I will eat it up. Is there even any information in <b>The Realm</b> that is not made-up trivia?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's all made up trivia, but 2nd edition did give rise to some significant rifts in people's interpretations of what Creation looks like on the ground level because of what it chose to focus on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T15:24:16-07:00","id":1446353,"title":"","content":"One example that stuck out for me during a flip-through of CoTD West was how Buruku, the &quot;first among equals&quot; captain of the Wavecrest Navy was handled. In 1e, in Savage Seas, he is presented as being very possibly the descendant of one or more gods, and his preference for men was noted rather neutrally, as the various preferences of other figures in the chapter typically had been, with none apparently taking issue over it. In 2e, they made him the definite child of Wavecrest's main volcano god Hamoji, and the priesthood was embarrassed that he was gay because they wanted to play Bene Gesserit with lines of god-blooded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-28T19:02:45-07:00","id":1446389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1446353#post1446353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One example that stuck out for me during a flip-through of CoTD West was how Buruku, the &quot;first among equals&quot; captain of the Wavecrest Navy was handled. In 1e, in Savage Seas, he is presented as being very possibly the descendant of one or more gods, and his preference for men was noted rather neutrally, as the various preferences of other figures in the chapter typically had been, with none apparently taking issue over it. In 2e, they made him the definite child of Wavecrest's main volcano god Hamoji, and the priesthood was embarrassed that he was gay because they wanted to play Bene Gesserit with lines of god-blooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, 2e also had the problem of &quot;the greatest utility of lesser supernaturals is their capacity to produce magical children.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-29T03:48:18-07:00","id":1446428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1446389#post1446389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, 2e also had the problem of &amp;quot;the greatest utility of lesser supernaturals is their capacity to produce magical children.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>2e had a lot of issues like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-01T18:48:27-07:00","id":1446886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1446389#post1446389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, 2e also had the problem of &quot;the greatest utility of lesser supernaturals is their capacity to produce magical children.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>And its corollary problem, &quot;bloodlines of lesser supernaturals must be kept pure at all cost, even if it involves utterly heartless culling.&quot; The edition comes off as un-ironically accepting the Lintha Book of Utz Semivir.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T13:54:01-07:00","id":1447260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1446428#post1446428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2e had a lot of issues like that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Remember how Dragon Blooded became such non-exalts you could make a manse that mass produced them with every single child produced in your happy fun times eugenics camp guaranteed to be dragon blooded because it somehow got into the books that there was a surefire method to ensure your kid would become one (and therefore be doomed to never be one of the real exalted)? Though I guess I'm not sure eugenics is the correct word since, IIRC, the method had more to do with the mother bathing in elemental manse energy while pregnant and bribing a god that apparently controls dragon blooded exaltation then it had anything to do with genetics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T16:02:58-07:00","id":1447289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1447260#post1447260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Remember how Dragon Blooded became such non-exalts you could make a manse that mass produced them with every single child produced in your happy fun times eugenics camp guaranteed to be dragon blooded because it somehow got into the books that there was a surefire method to ensure your kid would become one (and therefore be doomed to never be one of the real exalted)? Though I guess I'm not sure eugenics is the correct word since, IIRC, the method had more to do with the mother bathing in elemental manse energy while pregnant and bribing a god that apparently controls dragon blooded exaltation then it had anything to do with genetics.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doomed to never be a real exalt in 2e was fucking so out of place. In that edition, there weren't even exigents so there were literally 700 celestial exalts. 100 of which could only be chosen at birth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T17:23:55-07:00","id":1447305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1447289#post1447289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That doomed to never be a real exalt in 2e was fucking so out of place. In that edition, there weren't even exigents so there were literally 700 celestial exalts. 100 of which could only be chosen at birth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, the bit in Yu-Shan about gods innately disrespecting dragon blooded on a fundamental level that could never be overcome no matter what compared to the respect they gave to mortals because a mortal at least had an infinitesimal chance of becoming a real exalt someday was the funniest thing in the whole edition. It was so stupidly ridiculous in how ham fisted it was being in shitting on the dragon blooded but it also didn't think things through and made the hilarious joke that gods<u><i> innately respect mortals.</i></u>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T17:47:41-07:00","id":1447310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1447260#post1447260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Remember how Dragon Blooded became such non-exalts you could make a manse that mass produced them with every single child produced in your happy fun times eugenics camp guaranteed to be dragon blooded because it somehow got into the books that there was a surefire method to ensure your kid would become one (and therefore be doomed to never be one of the real exalted)? Though I guess I'm not sure eugenics is the correct word since, IIRC, the method had more to do with the mother bathing in elemental manse energy while pregnant and bribing a god that apparently controls dragon blooded exaltation then it had anything to do with genetics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like... this was one guy's one obsession, and based on a very liberal interpretation of how manse powered time dilation could work. This was not how the text of the game portrayed anything.<br /> <br /> I can't recall offhand if there was a mechanic for guaranteeing Exaltation rather than just improving the odds, but I think it's fair to say that its own context probably intended it to be only slightly less onerous than completing the Caul pilgrimage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 05-03-2021, 08:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T18:07:07-07:00","id":1447313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1447305#post1447305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, the bit in Yu-Shan about gods innately disrespecting dragon blooded on a fundamental level that could never be overcome no matter what compared to the respect they gave to mortals because a mortal at least had an infinitesimal chance of becoming a real exalt someday was the funniest thing in the whole edition. It was so stupidly ridiculous in how ham fisted it was being in shitting on the dragon blooded but it also didn't think things through and made the hilarious joke that gods<u><i> innately respect mortals.</i></u></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. That was a weird sidebar. A lot of them were weird sidebars though. Still better than infernals fluff which, lilun's not even the worst part about that. I think people brush it aside but infernals exalt and then get soul raped by the yozi's third circle demons and that's not really talked about much when people remember the infernals book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T18:08:35-07:00","id":1447314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1447310#post1447310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like... this was one guy's one obsession, and based on a very liberal interpretation of how manse powered time dilation could work. This was not how the text of the game portrayed anything.<br /> <br /> I can't recall offhand if there was a mechanic for guaranteeing Exaltation rather than just improving the odds, but I think it's fair to say that its own context probably intended it to be only slightly less onerous than completing the Caul pilgrimage.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I can't find the links to those crazy game breaking manses they liked making but I don't recall them using home brew, just official published stuff that was poorly thought through in a way not uncommon in 2E. Will have to look into it after work and see if I can find it or find the stuff they built it with (something that broken was probably in Dreams).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 05-03-2021, 09:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T20:59:16-07:00","id":1447329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1447310#post1447310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like... this was one guy's one obsession, and based on a very liberal interpretation of how manse powered time dilation could work. This was not how the text of the game portrayed anything.<br /> <br /> I can't recall offhand if there was a mechanic for guaranteeing Exaltation rather than just improving the odds, but I think it's fair to say that its own context probably intended it to be only slightly less onerous than completing the Caul pilgrimage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also just a general reminder that if the mechanics make it seem like the setting doesn't make sense, the mechanics are wrong and the setting is right.<br /> <br /> Like if there was a merit published in Nightmares from the Depths that said &quot;this character has mutated lung capacity, for all purposes treat them as facing infinite rounds before suffocation. This is a very common mutation among the people of the deep western sea, though it is distinct from Gills, as it does not require water, or anything, to breathe.&quot;<br /> <br /> Then a spell from Three Circles that said &quot;Air is everything. While this spell is active on a cursed target any physical damage, from an attack, environment or even poison, does not get resolved normally, but rather removes a number of rounds of suffocation equal to the value. Likewise social influence is not resolved normally, treat the character's resolve/guile as being equal to their rounds of suffocation, unmodified by intimacies. Also treat their base dicepool for any action as equal to their rounds of suffocation, unless they spend a willpower to overcome the effect. This curse lasts until the cursed target successfully resists it, they may try once per scene. Only mortal beings can be affected by such a terrible curse.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> The response to that isn't to go, well, damn, I guess mortals are the real power in Creation. One tiny group of people with that mutation and a sorcerer with that spell would be unstoppable. Immune to damage, infinite dicepools, infinite static values, it's strange that Exalted history went by as it did without this cropping up. I either need to change it so the whole world is run by a secret cabal of infinite dicepol water-people, or right from the start this new unstoppable empire will rise in my game.<br /> <br /> That's obviously totally stupid, no mortal with a common merit and terrestrial circle curse cast on them should be able to backhand the unconqured sun into a wall. That extends to other things too. The Lunar charmset makes it look like infiltrating the Imperial Palace or the Bureau of Destiny should be an effortless cakewalk? They have defences against that, it doesn't matter if they're printed as having them, they have them, either that or the charms can't work like they say they do. Two weird DB charms combo together to give you an infinitely large and perfectly loyal army of Raksha? No they don't. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1447314#post1447314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I can't find the links to those crazy game breaking manses they liked making but I don't recall them using home brew, just official published stuff that was poorly thought through in a way not uncommon in 2E. Will have to look into it after work and see if I can find it or find the stuff they built it with (something that broken was probably in Dreams).</div> </div> </div> </div>The funny thing was in 2e having an infinitely large army of DBs wasn't even that helpful. They couldn't actually hurt any of the major players in a fight or in social combat, and they got cut down like wheat. Mechanically anyway, from a setting standpoint if you had an army of 100,000 dragonblooded you'd smash through Creations greatest armies like a hammer through a teapot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T09:36:34-07:00","id":1447415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1447314#post1447314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't find the links to those crazy game breaking manses they liked making but I don't recall them using home brew</div> </div> </div> </div>I did not say home brew, I said liberal interpretation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">just official published stuff that was poorly thought through in a way not uncommon in 2E.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not even that, really. If I recall it correctly, it basically went &quot;a manse can be used to create a Wyld Zone, Wyld Zones have time dilation with unspecified parameters, ergo t'ain't no rule saying a dog can't build a manse where fifteen years pass in a day&quot;. That's not poorly thought through so much as there being an intent for cultivated Wyld Zones, and even a Rip van Winkle effect, other than how a particular person applied them.<br /> <br /> Although perhaps there was an alternative based on the manse accelerating growth rates, but even that can be reasonably assumed to have not been particularly intended for going from baby to adult in extremely convenient manner.<br /> <br /> The biggest thing that can be laid on the feet of the books was stating that elemental parentage guaranteed Exaltation. That's at least a poorly thought out detail in a generally maligned book.<br /> <br /> But the key thing here is that it is unwarranted to imply this whole thing was a Second Edition issue rather than coming from a particular person's interests. Frankly, while Second Edition had its issues, including for the Dragon Blooded, I think some of their expression in the moment and the enduring memory of such had a lack of perspective.<br /> <br /> I mean, even as far as the Yu-Shan stuff went... was the idea that the Celestial Gods were supposed to be jerks too subtle for folks? I can understand people having an objection to the idea of that particular kind of prejudice being held by those kinds of characters, but it goes way beyond when there are people acting like it was writing meant to convey a hostile attitude for Dragon Blooded in objective first person, or that gods in this setting are meant to be read as guides for moral truth. I think a good faith reading would at least entertain the idea that the statement was intended less as the writers sneering at Terrestrials and more as them sincerely attempting to write jerk gods being jerks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 05-04-2021, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T11:07:49-07:00","id":1447420,"title":"","content":"A Dragon-Blooded parent and a supernatural (say, a nymph) guaranteed Dragon-Blooded offspring in 2E.<br /> <br /> Which completely cut out the Right Hand of Power (Lytec) who decides whether your kid Exalts. Then you just have to bribe the Left Hand of Power (The God of Inherited Might) to get your Breeding 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 05-04-2021, 02:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T13:00:41-07:00","id":1447437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1447415#post1447415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I did not say home brew, I said liberal interpretation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Not even that, really. If I recall it correctly, it basically went &quot;a manse can be used to create a Wyld Zone, Wyld Zones have time dilation with unspecified parameters, ergo t'ain't no rule saying a dog can't build a manse where fifteen years pass in a day&quot;. That's not poorly thought through so much as there being an intent for cultivated Wyld Zones, and even a Rip van Winkle effect, other than how a particular person applied them.<br /> <br /> Although perhaps there was an alternative based on the manse accelerating growth rates, but even that can be reasonably assumed to have not been particularly intended for going from baby to adult in extremely convenient manner.<br /> <br /> The biggest thing that can be laid on the feet of the books was stating that elemental parentage guaranteed Exaltation. That's at least a poorly thought out detail in a generally maligned book.<br /> <br /> But the key thing here is that it is unwarranted to imply this whole thing was a Second Edition issue rather than coming from a particular person's interests. Frankly, while Second Edition had its issues, including for the Dragon Blooded, I think some of their expression in the moment and the enduring memory of such had a lack of perspective.<br /> <br /> I mean, even as far as the Yu-Shan stuff went... was the idea that the Celestial Gods were supposed to be jerks too subtle for folks? I can understand people having an objection to the idea of that particular kind of prejudice being held by those kinds of characters, but it goes way beyond when there are people acting like it was writing meant to convey a hostile attitude for Dragon Blooded in objective first person, or that gods in this setting are meant to be read as guides for moral truth. I think a good faith reading would at least entertain the idea that the statement was intended less as the writers sneering at Terrestrials and more as them sincerely attempting to write jerk gods being jerks.</div> </div> </div> </div>The part where they dilated time to pump them out fast was kinda 'don't think they intended that' but it was stated outright that you could guarantee your child would exalt as opposed to it being the mixing of several mechanics together.<br /> <br /> .....Have you read that sidebar lately? because it did exactly those things. It literally was written as an objective statement that it was a fact of reality that dragon blooded are dastardly usurpers and solars are the true and correct rulers of Creation. Like, it literally called it an objective fact literally written into the very fabric of reality by the creation ruling mandate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As the Bronze Faction can attest, most gods<br /> seem to have a visceral contempt for the Dragon-<br /> Blooded. A few gods, mainly gods intimately<br /> connected to the Scarlet Empire such as Gri-Fel,<br /> are staunch supporters of the Bronze Faction and<br /> the Immaculate Order, but for the most part,<br /> this loyalty is self-serving\u2014Gri-Fel, the God of<br /> the Imperial City, cannot meaningfully oppose<br /> the Immaculate Order without undermining<br /> the source of all his power. In contrast to Gri-<br /> Fel, Jagalza, the Satrap of the Realm, supports<br /> the Bronze Faction only reluctantly due to the<br /> requirements of her office, and she does little<br /> to hide her disdain for Dragon-Blooded.<br /> Most of the Bronze Faction members think<br /> that this disdain is simply a holdover from the<br /> Usurpation, as well as the rather indelicate manner<br /> in which the Immaculate Order asserts the<br /> dominance of the Dragon-Blooded over the Terrestrial<br /> gods.<u> They are mistaken, for the antipathy<br /> runs much deeper than that.<br /> The truth of the matter lies in the Creation-<br /> Ruling Mandate handed down by the<br /> Unconquered Sun to his Exalted children, establishing<br /> the inherent right of the Solar Exalted to<br /> rule in his name. Although the Mandate was the<br /> Unconquered Sun\u2019s to hand down, the Mandate<br /> also had the support of the other Incarnae, and<br /> as a result, the right to rule became inherent in<br /> the Celestial Exalted, and this right was woven<br /> into the very fabric of Creation. Consequently,<br /> it was woven into the very fabric of the gods,<br /> as well.<br /> As a result, all gods, even those who supported<br /> the Usurpation whether for altruistic<br /> or selfish reasons, instinctively know that the<br /> Usurpation defied the natural order, which<br /> demands that the Celestial Exalted rule Creation.</u><br /> Dragon-Blooded may have ruled Creation<br /> during the Shogunate, and they may yet rule<br /> all Creation again. But for all their power and<br /> wealth and influence, no Dragon-Blood will<br /> ever hold the respect that a god will instinctively<br /> have for the lowliest street urchin. It<br /> is possible, however unlikely, that the dirty<br /> street urchin might someday receive Celestial<br /> Exaltation. By their very natures, no Dragon-<br /> Blood ever will. </div> </div> </div>I mean, this is garbage nonsense on so many levels and its easy to poke holes in it like 'gods innately respect mortals? Pull the other one its got bells on it' but it is still an officially published 'fact' that objective reality is saying dragon blooded are trash lower then even mortals because mortals have a slight chance of someday being a 'real exalt' and that its a fact of reality that celestial exalts are the true rightful rulers of Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 05-04-2021, 05:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T17:03:58-07:00","id":1447490,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I never got some of the fan hate for the gods looking down on Terrestrials, actually, as a basic thing. I mean I can get people saying that it was a poor and stupid execution of the idea in 2e, but the Celestial gods are, while genuinely numinous, also a combination of the shallow, selfish gods of Dunsany with a snobbish, out of touch bureaucratic elite, and their rose-tinted takes on the First Age reflects more than a little how its prosperity benefitted their appetites rather than any high moral purpose. Their disfavour is a mixed dishonor to say they least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T17:43:37-07:00","id":1447497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1447490#post1447490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I never got some of the fan hate for the gods looking down on Terrestrials, actually, as a basic thing. I mean I can get people saying that it was a poor and stupid execution of the idea in 2e, but the Celestial gods are, while genuinely numinous, also a combination of the shallow, selfish gods of Dunsany with a snobbish, out of touch bureaucratic elite, and their rose-tinted takes on the First Age reflects more than a little how its prosperity benefitted their appetites rather than any high moral purpose. Their disfavour is a mixed dishonor to say they least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it came with the assertion that they were objectively correct and that it was a metaphysical fact of reality woven into the very fabric of existence as opposed to being written as them just being snobs who look down on them for being upjumped monkeys that can belch fire or whatever? And that Compass:Yu Shan was just the most hilariously ham fisted and egregious way 2E treated dragon blooded like a joke so its not like people bring it up in a vacuum. Especially once 2E started focusing on elder essence stuff later in the cycle and just didn't even bother pretending anymore that dragon blooded mattered when you should really be going out and punching Malfeas in the face or slam dunking elder essence solar ghosts into Oblivion instead (and not think too hard on stuff like how the hell the Usurpation even happened successfully in the current paradigm).<br /> <br /> <br /> 2E was my first go at Exalted and I still like it but it had some notable issues keeping things coherent and in how it treated some demographics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T17:48:39-07:00","id":1447498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1447497#post1447497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because it came with the assertion that they were objectively correct and that it was a metaphysical fact of reality woven into the very fabric of existence as opposed to being written as them just being snobs who look down on them for being upjumped monkeys that can belch fire or whatever? And that Compass:Yu Shan was just the most hilariously ham fisted and egregious way 2E treated dragon blooded like a joke so its not like people bring it up in a vacuum. Especially once 2E started focusing on elder essence stuff later in the cycle and just didn't even bother pretending anymore that dragon blooded mattered when you should really be going out and punching Malfeas in the face or slam dunking elder essence solar ghosts into Oblivion instead (and not think too hard on stuff like how the hell the Usurpation even happened successfully in the current paradigm).<br /> <br /> <br /> 2E was my first go at Exalted and I still like it but it had so notable issues keeping things coherent and in how it treated some demographics.</div> </div> </div> </div>2E was my first go too and I just can't even look at it anymore outside of the alchemicals book. There's just too many issues with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T18:27:03-07:00","id":1447506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1447498#post1447498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2E was my first go too and I just can't even look at it anymore outside of the alchemicals book. There's just too many issues with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still find a lot of the fluff enjoyable and evocative, though I don't have an exact ratio on how much of it is so. Maybe once work slows down I can go back and do something like reread it and see how much exactly I like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T00:37:30-07:00","id":1447532,"title":"","content":"I actually laughed out loud re-reading that sidebar. &quot;Yes, this is Exalted, a game where we don't shy away from the ugly side of empire building, and the corruptive influence of power...but also totally the divine right of kings is real and true, and every god knows that the ones chosen by god are the rightful rulers and it upsets them to see otherwise.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T00:48:49-07:00","id":1447535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1447532#post1447532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually laughed out loud re-reading that sidebar. &quot;Yes, this is Exalted, a game where we don't shy away from the ugly side of empire building, and the corruptive influence of power...but also totally the divine right of kings is real and true, and every god knows that the ones chosen by god are the rightful rulers and it upsets them to see otherwise.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why those two are mutually exclusive. There can be multiple kings with divine rights and things can get ugly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T01:33:22-07:00","id":1447543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1447535#post1447535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see why those two are mutually exclusive. There can be multiple kings with divine rights and things can get ugly.</div> </div> </div> </div>in-universe they might not be, but tonally they are. The Solars are chosen by God to rule, you may not question their authority, for their right to dominate lesser beings has been ordained by the highest power, and is a metaphysical truth of Creation. That's the exact reasoning that absolute monarchs and dictators have used for millennia on real Earth. Pharaohs, emperors and kings have killed people for daring to question their rule, because to question their rule is to question god, and that is a sin. A king doesn't need the consent of the people he's ruling, every one of them could despise him and still it would be wrong to replace him because god wills that he rule.<br /> <br /> Which could be fine for a fantasy world, sure, but every other blatant lie used by corrupt powerful people to keep power in the real world isn't true in Exalted. The Realm isn't a shining example of culture that uses its immense power to raise up the unfortunate kingdoms of the Threshold and give them a better life, that's just, basically, a lie told by empires to justify why they should rule you, and you shouldn't rule yourself. In Exalted the rebels fighting their government aren't pure and innocent freedom lovers who never kill anyone that doesn't deserve it, and will make everything better for sure just as soon as they get to be in power. <br /> <br /> But then we get to the divine right of kings as it pertains to the celestial Exalted and suddenly yeah, no, that's totally how it works. If you're a king, and one of your subjects exalts Solar, you should abdicate and put them in charge. Doesn't matter if they're a cruel tyrant, or kind of a dumbass who's exaltation makes them an amazing sailor but kind of a shit negotiator/planner, it is their right to rule and you mustn't question it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T02:11:38-07:00","id":1447547,"title":"","content":"*raises hand*<br /> <br /> If I may point out, that Exalted doesn't exactly give two shits about the moral power of gods. An interpretation of the Unconquered Sun is that he's basically someone that's coked out, negligient, and basically doesn't give too much of a shit about the world. And another interpretation is that the Exaltations are superweapons set loose onto the world, never to be held down save by great immense effort. The Unconquered Sun is <b>Lucifer</b>, the MorningStar who rose up against his creator, and won. He then bequeathed the Mandate of Heaven upon the Exalted, having wrested it from the Primordials.<br /> <br /> Yes, in Exalted, there is literally divine power floating around, latching around to souls whom the highest and most mighty god of all decide have his favor. Yes, the very laws of metaphysics scream and declare that these people have the right to rule. Yes, their powers are incredible and even the weakest Dragonblooded is an deadly and powerful being. Yes, the gods declare that these have the Mandate.<br /> <br /> But that doesn't mean jack shit. The Mandate was from the Primordials, whom the King of Heaven wrested from their bloodied hands right before fucking off to the X-box and cocaine. The gods are rarely good, at best apathetic, and most of all venal, greedy, and capricious. Being in their favor doesn't mean jack shit, because in the end they were divine bureaucrats who were former slaves, and have little to no moral authority in their own. The Big Good of the setting has my props for not being totally evil, but apathy and overlooking the corruption of Heaven is a sin in and of itself.<br /> <br /> In other words: There is no contradiction to the other things in Exalted (The Realm, Rebels, etc) because yes, they have divine right of kings. But divine right of kings is dependent on the gods being the ultimate moral authority, and when they don't have that, the entire thing crumbles.<br /> <br /> edit: Tl;dr fuck the divine right of kings, murder the gods and topple their thrones","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T05:52:45-07:00","id":1447567,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s true, but what changes it is that it\u2019s not just the gods being dicks. If it was just the gods being classy assholes who refuse to accept that anyone but a celestial exalt has rights, that\u2019s one thing, but the sidebar isn\u2019t saying that. Specifically it\u2019s saying that even the gods who supported the usurpation can not, no matter how he\u2019d they try, ever REALLY respect a terrestrial exalt, because it is woven into the very fabric of reality that they are to be servants to their betters. Water flows, stars shine, the things that die are gone forever, and the celestial exalted have the right to rule over all others, each of these is a fact of Creation. If a Solar was in charge, the gods would likely still be dicks but at least you could theoretically convince them not to be. With a Dragonblooded in charge they physically can not be content, because a servant being in charge is just wrong, and nothing will ever be truly right until they get back in their place.<br /> <br /> Which I think just isn\u2019t good for Exalted. It can be fine in other media, but in Creation it just sticks out as desperate from everything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 05-05-2021, 08:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T09:21:09-07:00","id":1447585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1447567#post1447567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2019s true, but what changes it is that it\u2019s not just the gods being dicks. If it was just the gods being classy assholes who refuse to accept that anyone but a celestial exalt has rights, that\u2019s one thing, but the sidebar isn\u2019t saying that. Specifically it\u2019s saying that even the gods who supported the usurpation can not, no matter how he\u2019d they try, ever REALLY respect a terrestrial exalt, because it is woven into the very fabric of reality that they are to be servants to their betters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Notice, that, by the same reasoning, gods cannot respect themselves, because it is woven in the fabric of reality that they, too, are servants to their betters. And that it's Primordials that are those betters.<br /> The same Primordials they happened to defeat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1447567#post1447567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Water flows, stars shine, the things that die are gone forever, and the celestial exalted have the right to rule over all others, each of these is a fact of Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>So is the fact that a Primordial cannot be slain. And, yet again, facts of Creation happen to not be so unmutable as it may seem.<br /> <br /> And of course there's that tiny little case of Gods giving out the Mandate to Exalted at least partially because they preferred to give it willingly, and not wait till the weapons they created decide to wrestle that mandate from their cold (and very, very dead) divine hands.<br /> <br /> I mean, yes, that sidebar was bad, and someone should be ashamed for writing it, but we should still consider it within the context of the game.<br /> <br /> And the context of this game is that:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1447547#post1447547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">fuck the divine right of kings, murder the gods and topple their thrones</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T09:57:08-07:00","id":1447594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1447585#post1447585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Notice, that, by the same reasoning, gods cannot respect themselves, because it is woven in the fabric of reality that they, too, are servants to their betters. And that it's Primordials that are those betters.<br /> The same Primordials they happened to defeat.<br /> <br /> So is the fact that a Primordial cannot be slain. And, yet again, facts of Creation happen to not be so unmutable as it may seem.<br /> <br /> And of course there's that tiny little case of Gods giving out the Mandate to Exalted at least partially because they preferred to give it willingly, and not wait till the weapons they created decide to wrestle that mandate from their cold (and very, very dead) divine hands.<br /> <br /> I mean, yes, that sidebar was bad, and someone should be ashamed for writing it, but we should still consider it within the context of the game.<br /> <br /> And the context of this game is that:<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Imagine if it was for some other injustice though. Like the underpinnings of reality in Creation are entwined with the truth that no woman may have authority over any man, and thus no spirit or god can ever be brought to truly respect the Scarlet Empress. However, with unthinkable effort, and the combined will of the entire exalted host, it may be possible to tear apart the fabric of reality, and unweave that axiomatic truth. In so doing it would at least be possible to afford the Empress the same implicit respect given to even the lowest man. <br /> <br /> Except the sidebar doesn\u2019t even say that, it just says gods implicitly respect men and not women because it\u2019s a truth of Creation than men shall have the right to rule. It\u2019s just so counter to everything else in the setting that doesn\u2019t give any over-arching moral system like DnD or something, on top of being a garbage system if it was.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: also it takes away from the gods being dicks about it. They don\u2019t respect the Empress because she\u2019s a DB, but it\u2019s not their fault, reality is bent around the concept that she is the servant class. They just can\u2019t help themselves, it\u2019s the natural order of things that she obey, not lead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 05-05-2021, 01:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T14:37:25-07:00","id":1447633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Notice, that, by the same reasoning, gods cannot respect themselves, because it is woven in the fabric of reality that they, too, are servants to their betters. And that it's Primordials that are those betters.<br /> The same Primordials they happened to defeat. </div> </div> </div>Yes, you are adequately explaining one of the reasons its a stupid thing to have claimed as an excuse to try and make it canon that all gods everywhere hold contempt for dragon blooded and it is impossible to change this. I didn't feel like making a list and just put out the funniest part (gods innately respect mortals and the celestial exalted) but that is another good reason it was a dumb side bar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So is the fact that a Primordial cannot be slain. And, yet again, facts of Creation happen to not be so unmutable as it may seem. </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure they never actually did anything of the sort, they just arrogantly assumed it was a fact of reality already and made no effort to set up any sort of further rules into the laws of reality stating that they couldn't die.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T15:40:34-07:00","id":1447646,"title":"","content":"To simplify the issue with 2e in terms of the solar supremacy, despite killing the rightful rulers of creation. Every statement in 2e about solars was a moral statement about how they were the rightful rulers of creation. Despite the fact that 1e never made such an objective moral claim. The bias at several points also causes 2e in several places to diminish the roles of other exalts to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-05T15:45:46-07:00","id":1447648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1441051-homosexuality-in-exalted-second-edition?p=1447646#post1447646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To simplify the issue with 2e in terms of the solar supremacy, despite killing the rightful rulers of creation. Every statement in 2e about solars was a moral statement about how they were the rightful rulers of creation. Despite the fact that 1e never made such an objective moral claim. The bias at several points also causes 2e in several places to diminish the roles of other exalts to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I can't remember 1e doing that at all. Demetheus even said in his backstory that well, if they got so mad at what we were doing they felt they had to murder us all, maybe we had it coming, maybe we need to do better next time, if we deserve a next time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}